      <!-- Section 3: JPG Size Reducer & Compress JPG -->
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-display-md text-[var(--color-ink)]">
          JPG Size Reducer: How to Compress JPG and Reduce JPG Size
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          JPEG remains the most universally recognized digital photo standard on the planet. However, modern high-megapixel smartphone cameras frequently generate raw JPEG files weighing between 6 MB and 18 MB. When preparing these photos for web publishing or messaging, utilizing a dedicated <strong>jpg size reducer</strong> is essential.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          When you <strong>compress jpg</strong> files using our engine, the algorithm applies Discrete Cosine Transform (DCT) block quantization and 4:2:0 chroma subsampling. This selectively removes high-frequency color variations that the human eye cannot perceive while preserving crisp focal edges, facial contours, and typography. As a result, you can <strong>reduce jpg size</strong> by 70% to 85% with zero perceptible distortion.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 4: Reduce Image Resolution vs Reduce Image Quality -->
