          How to Reduce Image Size Without Losing Quality
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The holy grail of image optimization is the ability to <strong>reduce image size without losing quality</strong>. How is this mathematically possible? Our in-browser compression engine achieves this through perceptual optimization:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>Metadata Elimination:</strong> Cameras attach hundreds of kilobytes of invisible EXIF data, including camera serial numbers, GPS coordinates, thumbnail caches, and exposure timestamps. Stripping these saves immediate bytes with zero visual penalty.</li>
          <li><strong>Perceptual Quantization:</strong> Human visual acuity is far more sensitive to variations in luminance (brightness) than chrominance (color). We compress chrominance channels more aggressively, leaving brightness contrast intact.</li>
          <li><strong>Bicubic Resampling:</strong> When scaling dimensions, high-order polynomial interpolation prevents pixelation and jagged stair-stepping edges along high-contrast lines.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Using our split comparison preview slider, you can verify before-and-after fidelity down to the individual pixel before saving your files.
        </p>
